   "subject": "Re: More than one detection per occasion in sim.capthist",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The default detector type in read.traps() is &#39;multi&#39; which refers to a multi-catch trap i.e. one that can catch multiple animals at once. With &#39;multi&#39; detectors there is never more than one detection per animal per occasion - that&#39;s in the nature of traps.</div><div><br></div><div>Use read.traps(.. detector = &#39;proximity&#39;) to allow the possibility of multiple detections on one occasion.</div><div><br></div><div>Check with table(apply(tch.F, 1:2, sum)) <br></div><div><br></div><div>I also suggest you play with secrdesignapp, or at least use it as a cross-check -<br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><pre><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>runGitHub</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span><span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#080\">secrdesignapp</span><span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span><span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#080\">MurrayEfford</span><span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></pre></div></code></div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
